    {
      "bbox": [
        340,
        1246,
        1977,
        1585
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Many agencies provide products and services (such as directories, searches, public record lists) for sale to the public. Some of these products and services are required by law; others are byproducts of the agency's operations. In a number of instances, prices are set by law (e.g., a list must be made available at the cost of reproducing it). When this is not the case, pricing policies vary greatly.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2603,
          "min": -1.3307
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 85,
          "mean": -0.0003,
          "min": -0.0086
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 4668,
        "area_px": 554200,
        "density": 0.00842,
        "chars": 402,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 86.12
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        346,
        1616,
        2014,
        1958
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "It has come to my attention that many agencies have not made a recent review of their costs and policies. Even where the pricing policy is set by law, price revision may be in order so that selling prices may be brought in line with current costs. Also it is probable that there are products and services now being provided free for which there should be a fee.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2624,
          "min": -1.5882
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 72,
          "mean": -0.001,
          "min": -0.0693
        }
      },
